SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine's Minimum Wage to Increase to $15.70 Pe
 r Hour in 2027
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Maine's Mini
 mum Wage to Increase to $15.70 Per Hour in 2027\nServices\nJobs & Training
 \nUnemployment Insurance\nDisability Services\nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Law
 s\nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nMaine's Minimum Wage to Increa
 se to $15.70 Per Hour in 2027\nSeptember 18\, 2026\nFor Immediate Release:
  September 18\, 2026\nMedia Contact: Autumn Mahoney\, Communications Speci
 alist\nmedia.dol@maine.gov\nAUGUSTA - The Maine Department of Labor announ
 ced today that\, effective\nJanuary 1\, 2027\n\, the state minimum wage wi
 ll increase from $15.10 to\n$15.70\nper hour\, based on data recently made
  available by the U.S. Department of Labor's Bureau of Labor Statistics. M
 DOL is required under Maine law (Maine statute Title 26\, chapter 7\, sect
 ion 664) to make annual adjustments to the minimum wage based on the cost-
 of-living index (CPI-W) for the Northeast Region\, after Maine voters amen
 ded the law by referendum in 2016. Between August 2025 and August 2026\, t
 here was a\n4.1\npercent increase in the CPI-W.\nAccording to the U.S. Dep
 artment of Labor's Bureau of Labor Statistics\nCurrent Population Survey f
 or  2025\n\, there were 28\,000 hourly workers who were paid less than $15
 .00 per hour. These workers represent about four percent of all wage and s
 alary workers (both paid at hourly rates and not paid at hourly rates) and
  about eight percent of wage and salary workers who are paid at hourly rat
 es.\nAgricultural workers in Maine are also entitled to the state minimum 
 wage\, after the Legislature enacted and Governor Mills signed "\nAn Act t
 o Establish a State Minimum Hourly Wage for Agricultural Workers\n" in 202
 5.\nThe "tip wage\," or service employee minimum wage\, will increase from
  $7.55 to\n$7.85 p\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?i
 d=13362373
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13362373
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
